1
00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:04,330
Every timeline you save to
a server starts private:

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:08,920
only you can open it. When it's
ready, its owner can make it public,

3
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:11,940
and then anyone can read
it, find it in search,

4
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:13,855
and follow its history.

5
00:00:15,565 --> 00:00:18,895
Share it with a link, to the
whole timeline, to one moment,

6
00:00:18,945 --> 00:00:23,945
or to exactly the view you're looking at.
Or embed it on your class page or your

7
00:00:23,995 --> 00:00:28,869
community's site, where readers can
explore it without leaving the page.

8
00:00:30,319 --> 00:00:34,589
Add collaborators by their
username, each with a role.

9
00:00:34,639 --> 00:00:40,629
A viewer can read a private timeline.
A contributor can propose changes.

10
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:45,559
A writer can save changes and
review what others propose.

11
00:00:45,609 --> 00:00:48,459
Only the owner decides
who's in, who can see it,

12
00:00:48,509 --> 00:00:50,494
and whether it's deleted.

13
00:00:52,224 --> 00:00:56,004
Students don't need to be
trusted with the whole timeline.

14
00:00:56,054 --> 00:00:59,634
As contributors, their
changes become pull requests:

15
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:03,334
a proposal showing what they
add, remove and change,

16
00:01:03,384 --> 00:01:07,084
with a discussion underneath.
A writer talks it through,

17
00:01:07,134 --> 00:01:11,304
then merges it or rejects
it. On a public timeline,

18
00:01:11,354 --> 00:01:13,928
anyone signed in can propose.

19
00:01:15,358 --> 00:01:22,478
Want to take it somewhere new? Fork it.
A fork is your own copy that remembers

20
00:01:22,528 --> 00:01:25,418
where it came from: bring in
the original's later changes,

21
00:01:25,468 --> 00:01:30,628
and offer yours back when they're ready.
Students without an account can fork it

22
00:01:30,678 --> 00:01:34,144
in the browser and export their work.

23
00:01:35,824 --> 00:01:39,804
When two people save at
once, their edits merge.

24
00:01:39,854 --> 00:01:43,894
Only when both changed the same thing
differently does it stop and ask whose to

25
00:01:43,944 --> 00:01:49,034
keep. And every save is a revision
in the timeline's history,

26
00:01:49,084 --> 00:01:51,741
so you can always go back to how it was.

27
00:01:53,291 --> 00:01:58,901
And if something doesn't belong, anyone
can report it to the site's moderators.

28
00:01:58,951 --> 00:02:01,831
Start a timeline, invite your
class or your community,

29
00:02:01,881 --> 00:02:03,506
and build it together.
